<title>USA: Chicago Bridge &amp; Iron IPO price range lowered.</title>
<headline>Chicago Bridge &amp; Iron IPO price range lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Bridge &amp; Iron Co NV's 10.5 million shares, scheduled to make their debut on the big board on Friday, are now expected to price within a lower range, according to lead underwriter CS First Boston.</p>
<p>The new pricing range is $19 to $20 a share, down from the earlier range of $20 to $23.</p>
<p>The company, a unit of Praxair Inc, is a provider of steel plate structures.</p>
